---
title: Vietnamese Style Sticky Shaking Beef
description: Seared tender steak tossed in a glossy-sweet glaze
servings: 2
course: Main
locale: en_GB
prep time: 20m
cook time: 5m
difficulty: Medium
cuisine: Vietnamese
tags:
- vietnamese
- savoury
- main-course
- meat
---

= Marinade Beef =

Put the @rump steak{500%g}(cut into bite-sized cubes) into a bowl with the marinade ingredients (@garlic{2%cloves}(finely chopped), @dark soy sauce{1%tbsp}, @fish sauce{1%tbsp}, @sugar{2%tsp}, and @black pepper{1%tsp}(ground)). Stir well and then set aside for ~{20%minutes}.

= Sauce =

Combine the sauce ingredients (@white wine vinegar{4%tbsp}, @oyster sauce{4%tbsp}, @water{4%tbsp}, @sugar{1%tbsp}) in a small bowl and set aside.

= Stir Fry Beef =

Heat a splash of oil in a non-stick frying pan over a high heat. When hot, add the marinated beef. Stir fry for ~{2%minutes} until it begins to caramelise.

Add three quarters of the @red onions{2}(finely sliced) to the pan and stir fry for ~{1%minute}.

Pour in the sauce and cook for a further ~{2%minutes}.

Turn down the heat and quickly stir in the @cornflour{1%tbsp}(mixed to a paste with a little water) to thicken the sauce, making sure there are no lumps.

Serve the sticky beef with rice and the remaining red onion scattered on top.